# --- bromigOS: the whole desktop (the meta-package pulls in every piece and its
# dependencies: Hyprland, the bar, the live layer, VECTOR, the login screen, fonts)
bromigos-keyring
bromigos
# optional pieces the installer offers (they're on the medium either way)
bromigos-homelab
herdr
# Field Kit, the edition with no desktop (its packages: the edition file, editions/fieldkit.json)
bromigos-lab
# the live desktop's and the installed system's extras bromigOS's defaults expect
btop
pavucontrol
pcmanfm
swappy
wf-recorder
brightnessctl
zoxide
bluez
bluez-utils
# Field Kit, the boot menu's "Field Kit (repair, lab and tools)" (docs/fieldkit.md): its engine
# and the tools its menu runs that releng's list doesn't have
bromigos-fieldkit-tools
partclone
chntpw
ntfs-3g
micro
htop
nvtop
gdu
inxi
iperf3
mtr
# the installed system: network, boot (GRUB), the disk (btrfs on LUKS2) and its snapshots
networkmanager
plymouth
grub
efibootmgr
grub-btrfs
inotify-tools
btrfs-progs
cryptsetup
snapper
snap-pac
# the installer: the graphical one (GTK 4 and libadwaita come with the desktop), the text one
# (Textual), and installing beside another system: other systems found for the boot menu,
# Windows' NTFS read and shrunk
python-textual
os-prober
ntfs-3g
# VECTOR's voice guide in the text installer, where no PipeWire session runs: ffmpeg decodes
# its Opus clips for aplay (alsa-utils, above); the desktop already brings it
ffmpeg
# graphics: every open driver, so the live desktop renders on whatever is there
mesa
vulkan-radeon
vulkan-intel
vulkan-nouveau
xf86-video-amdgpu
libva-mesa-driver
